{"guide":{"questionsToConsider":["Should the quiz cover the whole world, or one region your players know, such as Europe or Africa?","Are your players new to flags or keen fans? Swap the maple leaf for a harder lookalike if they are experts.","Should a wrong pick in the Southern Cross round cost a point, or simply earn nothing?","Do you need an email for a prize draw, or is a first name on the scoreboard enough?"],"howToUseResponses":"Sort responses by score to find a winner or to see who needs more practice. Check which question most people missed: if it is a lookalike pair such as Denmark and Norway, it is a good teaching moment for the next lesson. The confidence rating next to each score shows who guessed well and who knew it.","customizeSteps":["Swap in flags from the region you are teaching or celebrating, keeping one point on each correct option.","Move the score bands so the top result still needs nearly every answer right once you change the question count.","Share the link or embed it on your site, and read the scores in the dashboard or export them to CSV."],"faqs":[{"q":"Why are the flags described in words instead of shown?","a":"Describing a flag makes players picture it, which is harder and more memorable than spotting it. It also works well in a chat, one flag at a time."},{"q":"Which national flag is not a rectangle?","a":"Nepal. Its flag is two stacked triangles, and it is the only national flag that is not rectangular."},{"q":"How is the flags quiz scored?","a":"Each correct answer is worth a point. In the Southern Cross round each right country adds a point and each wrong one takes a point away, and the total picks one of three results."},{"q":"Can I use this flag quiz in a classroom?","a":"Yes. Share one link with the class, ask for first names only, and go over the most-missed flags afterwards."}]},"doc":{"schemaVersion":9,"title":"Flags of the world quiz","description":"Nine scored flag questions, each flag described in words, from maple leaves to dragons.","blocks":[{"id":"blk_flagsof00","ref":"welcome","title":"Think you know your flags? I'll describe each one, you name the country. Nine rounds, and a result at the end.","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"buttonLabel":"Start","type":"welcome"},{"id":"blk_flagsof01","ref":"player","title":"What name should go on the scoreboard?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"short_text","unique":false,"minLength":0,"maxLength":40},{"id":"blk_flagsof02","ref":"maple_leaf","title":"A red maple leaf on a white square, with a red band on each side. Whose flag is it?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_canada","label":"Canada","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_peru","label":"Peru","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_austria","label":"Austria","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_lebanon","label":"Lebanon","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_flagsof03","ref":"not_rectangle","title":"Only one national flag is not a rectangle. It is two stacked red triangles with a blue border. Which country?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_bhutan","label":"Bhutan","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_nepal","label":"Nepal","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_sri_lanka","label":"Sri Lanka","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_maldives","label":"Maldives","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_flagsof04","ref":"cedar","title":"Which country's flag has a green cedar tree between two red stripes?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_cyprus","label":"Cyprus","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_jordan","label":"Jordan","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_lebanon","label":"Lebanon","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_israel","label":"Israel","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_flagsof05","ref":"nordic_cross","title":"A white cross on a red background, with the upright pushed toward the pole. Which country?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_switzerland","label":"Switzerland","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_norway","label":"Norway","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_denmark","label":"Denmark","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_finland","label":"Finland","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_flagsof06","ref":"red_disc","title":"Japan's flag is a red disc on white. Which country flies a red disc on dark green?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_bangladesh","label":"Bangladesh","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_pakistan","label":"Pakistan","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_palau","label":"Palau","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_laos","label":"Laos","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_flagsof07","ref":"southern_cross","title":"Which of these flags show the Southern Cross constellation? Pick all that apply.","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"multi_select","options":[{"id":"opt_australia","label":"Australia","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_chile","label":"Chile","image_key":null,"score":-1},{"id":"opt_new_zealand","label":"New Zealand","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_argentina","label":"Argentina","image_key":null,"score":-1},{"id":"opt_papua_new_guinea","label":"Papua New Guinea","image_key":null,"score":1}],"minSelections":1,"maxSelections":5,"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_flagsof08","ref":"dragon","title":"Which country's flag shows a white dragon across a yellow and orange field?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_china